# Everything that is not the running application.
#
# Two of these matter more than tidiness. The root requirements.txt pulls in
# faster-whisper, torch and scipy — some 800 MB that this host has no use for
# and no room for — and the Python builder will use it if it finds it, so it
# is kept out and api/requirements.txt is the only one left to find. And the
# markdown files name real sellers and buyers, which is nobody's business at
# a public URL.

# --- never publish: third-party business records ---
data/
Invoices/
samples/
tests/
.env
*.pdf

# --- the voice stack does not run on this host ---
app/voice/
app/api/voice.py
app/templates/speak.html
app/templates/training.html
app/templates/trades.html

# --- would shadow api/requirements.txt and blow the bundle ---
# Anchored to the root. These patterns carry no slash, and an unanchored
# pattern matches at every level — so a bare `requirements.txt` took
# api/requirements.txt with it, leaving the builder nothing to install and
# every request failing on the first import.
/requirements.txt
/requirements-training.txt

# --- documentation, naming real parties ---
README.md
EXTRACTION_PLAN.md
DEPLOY-VERCEL.md

# --- local junk ---
.venv/
.DS_Store
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.gitignore
run.sh
scripts/
